//
// Phase J7a operator gate: norm_tail.
//
// The norm tail -- add, LayerNorm, gamma scale -- as three herds in one
// segment joined by L1->L1 channels, with x and residual packed into one L3
// buffer so the segment holds two shim MM2S streams per column and never
// enters the packet path. Same function as addnorm's pre-add form, checked
// against the same FP32 oracle; what this gate adds is the dataflow: the sum
// and the normalized tensor stay resident in L1 instead of round-tripping
// through L3 the way pattern/fused's decomposed tail does.
//
// Two shapes: 128x768, two trips per tile, cheap enough to carry the standing
// negative control; and the block's own 4096x768, 128 trips per tile, where
// the phase's precision claim is measured (mean_rel_L1 4.478e-3 against the
// decomposed tail's whole-layer 1.806e-2 -- see opcheck_specs.py for the
// measurements behind the tolerance).
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against an FP32 reference: np.isclose over the
// full output at rtol=1.6e-2, zero permitted mismatches. The inputs are drawn
// asymmetrically (x and residual from different distributions) so that a
// plane-addressing bug in the packed fetch cannot hide behind LayerNorm's
// scale invariance.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipe below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// xclbin load and dispatch -- the same inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution
// and KernelCache take, so this interlocks with every other NPU job in the
// repository. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would
// DEADLOCK against the gate command that invokes this suite.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_norm_tail_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_norm_tail_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-norm-tail PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// Both lines per shape, not just the verdict: the first is XRTRunner's own,
// the second names the operator and shape, so a test wired to the wrong
// operator fails here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] norm_tail [128x768]: PASS
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] norm_tail [4096x768]: PASS
